§§ `Rule 17 -- documents to be filed in an appeal to the General Division`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Twins: `o 19 r 17(4) the appellant's document is filed and served in time`, `o 19 r 17(8) the respondent's document is filed and served in time`,
-- `o 19 r 17(10) the appellant's reply document is filed and served in time`, `o 19 r 17(5) the appeal is deemed withdrawn`, `o 19 r 17(9) the respondent is barred from making submissions at the hearing of the appeal` (roc4-order-19-div-2.l4).
-- The clock of each step starts when the step before it is done: the appellant's 28 days run from the day the Registry informs the parties (trace time 0),
-- the respondent's 28 days from the day the appellant serves, and the Reply's 14 days from the day the respondent's Case is served.
-- "Unless the appellate Court otherwise orders" (paragraphs (5) and (9)) is an order outside the Rules, so the traces do not model it; the decision functions take it as an input.
-- src:2386 | (4) The appellant must file and serve — ( a )
-- src:2387 | the record of appeal;
-- src:2388 | ( b )
-- src:2389 | the appellant’s Case;
-- src:2390 | ( c )
-- src:2391 | the appellant’s core bundle of documents, with the written judgment or grounds of decision of the lower Court and the extracted order of the lower Court in a separate volume; and
-- src:2392 | ( d )
-- src:2393 | the appellant’s bundle of authorities,
-- src:2394 | within 28 days after the date on which the Registry informs the parties that the record of proceedings is available.
-- src:2395 | (5) Where the appellant fails to file and serve the record of appeal, the core bundle of documents or the appellant’s Case within the specified time, the appeal is deemed withdrawn unless the appellate Court otherwise orders.
-- src:2396 | (6) Where an appeal is deemed withdrawn pursuant to paragraph (5) and if all the parties to the appeal consent to the payment of the security for costs provided under Rule 16 to the appellant or the respondent, the appellant or the respondent (as the case may be) must file the document signifying such consent signed by the parties and in such event, the security for costs provided under Rule 16 must be paid to the appellant or the respondent (as the case may be) and any solicitor’s undertaking is discharged.
-- src:2397 | (7) Where an appeal is deemed withdrawn pursuant to paragraph (5) and if there are any outstanding issues as to costs or other matters that remain between the parties to the appeal — ( a )
-- src:2398 | the appellant or any party to the appeal may, within 14 days after the date that the appeal is deemed withdrawn, request in writing to the General Division for directions on those issues;
-- src:2399 | ( b )
-- src:2400 | no oral arguments are to be made in a request under sub‑paragraph ( a ) unless the appellate Court otherwise directs; and
-- src:2401 | ( c )
-- src:2402 | the Registrar of the Supreme Court may, upon receiving a request under sub‑paragraph ( a ), give directions on the making of written submissions for the request.
-- src:2403 | (8) The respondent must file and serve — ( a )
-- src:2404 | the respondent’s Case;
-- src:2405 | ( b )
-- src:2406 | the respondent’s core bundle of documents (if necessary); and
-- src:2407 | ( c )
-- src:2408 | the respondent’s bundle of authorities,
-- src:2409 | within 28 days after the appellant serves the documents mentioned in paragraph (4) on the respondent.
-- src:2410 | (9) Where the respondent fails to file and serve the respondent’s Case within the specified time, the respondent is not allowed to make submissions at the hearing of the appeal unless the appellate Court otherwise orders.
-- src:2411 | (10) The appellant must file and serve — ( a )
-- src:2412 | the appellant’s Reply (if any);
-- src:2413 | ( b )
-- src:2414 | the second core bundle (if necessary); and
-- src:2415 | ( c )
-- src:2416 | the appellant’s second bundle of authorities (if any),
-- src:2417 | within 14 days after the respondent’s Case is served on the appellant.
@ref O 19 r 17(4) (src:2386-2417)
GIVEN `o 19 r 17(10) there is a Reply, a second core bundle or a second bundle of authorities to file` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `o 19 duties party` `o 19 duties act`
`o 19 r 17(4) the appellant must file and serve the appellant's documents within 28 days and the respondent and the appellant must follow` MEANS
    PARTY `o 19 r 14(1) the appellant`
    MUST `o 19 r 17(4) file and serve the record of appeal, the appellant's Case, the appellant's core bundle of documents and the appellant's bundle of authorities`
    WITHIN 28
    HENCE (
        PARTY `o 19 r 17(8) the respondent`
        MUST `o 19 r 17(8) file and serve the respondent's Case, the respondent's core bundle of documents (if necessary) and the respondent's bundle of authorities`
        WITHIN 28
        HENCE (
            -- Paragraph (10) names only items "(if any)" and "(if necessary)": with none to file there is nothing to do, so the duty is asked only when there is something to file.
            IF `o 19 r 17(10) there is a Reply, a second core bundle or a second bundle of authorities to file`
            THEN (
                PARTY `o 19 r 14(1) the appellant`
                MUST `o 19 r 17(10) file and serve the appellant's Reply (if any), the second core bundle (if necessary) and the appellant's second bundle of authorities (if any)`
                WITHIN 14
                HENCE FULFILLED
                LEST BREACH BY `o 19 r 14(1) the appellant` BECAUSE "the appellant's Reply, second core bundle or second bundle of authorities was not filed and served within 14 days after the respondent's Case was served (rule 17(10)); the text gives no consequence for this"
            )
            ELSE FULFILLED
        )
        LEST BREACH BY `o 19 r 17(8) the respondent` BECAUSE "the respondent did not file and serve the respondent's Case within the specified time, so the respondent is not allowed to make submissions at the hearing of the appeal unless the appellate Court otherwise orders (rule 17(9)); this is the text's consequence, not a wrong"
    )
    LEST BREACH BY `o 19 r 14(1) the appellant` BECAUSE "the appellant did not file and serve the record of appeal, the core bundle of documents or the appellant's Case within the specified time, so the appeal is deemed withdrawn unless the appellate Court otherwise orders (rule 17(5)); this is the text's consequence, not a wrong"

