-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Twins: `o 19 r 15(1) the application for permission to the lower Court is made and served as required`, `o 19 r 15(3) the notice of appeal after permission is filed and served as required` (roc4-order-19-div-2.l4).
-- The time for paragraph (3) runs from the decision granting permission; trace time 0 is that day.
-- src:2360 | 15. —(1) Where permission to appeal is required, a party must apply for such permission from the lower Court and serve the application on all parties who have an interest in the appeal within 14 days after the date of the judgment. (2) Where the lower Court does not grant permission to appeal, the party may apply to the General Division for such permission and must serve the application on all parties who have an interest in the appeal within 14 days after the date of the lower Court’s decision not to grant permission.
@ref O 19 r 15(1) (src:2360)
