§§ `Rule 30 -- documents to be filed in an appeal to the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Twins: `o 19 r 30(4) the appellant's document is filed and served in time`, `o 19 r 30(5) the appellant's document on an appeal from the Appellate Division is filed and served in time`, `o 19 r 30(9) the respondent's document is filed and served in time`,
-- `o 19 r 30(11) the appellant's reply document is filed and served in time`, `o 19 r 30(6) the appeal is deemed withdrawn`, `o 19 r 30(10) the respondent is barred from making submissions at the hearing of the appeal` (roc4-order-19-div-3.l4).
-- This is the chain of rule 17 with 8 weeks (56 days) for the appellant in place of 28 days.
-- Paragraph (5) (an appeal from the Appellate Division) has the same 8 weeks and the same chain; only the first document differs (the supplemental record), so the first act names paragraph (4) or (5).
-- "Unless the appellate Court otherwise orders" (paragraphs (6) and (10)) is an order outside the Rules, so the traces do not model it; the decision functions take it as an input.
