-- src:2627 | (7) Where an appeal is deemed withdrawn pursuant to paragraph (6) and if all the parties to the appeal consent to the payment of the security for costs provided under Rule 27 to the appellant or the respondent, the appellant or the respondent (as the case may be) must file the document signifying such consent signed by the parties and in such event, the security for costs provided under Rule 27 must be paid to the appellant or the respondent (as the case may be) and any solicitor’s undertaking is discharged.
-- src:2628 | (8) Where an appeal is deemed withdrawn pursuant to paragraph (6) and if there are any outstanding issues as to costs or other matters that remain between the parties to the appeal — ( a )
-- src:2629 | the appellant or any party to the appeal may, within 14 days after the date that the appeal is deemed withdrawn, request in writing to the appellate Court for directions on those issues;
-- src:2630 | ( b )
-- src:2631 | no oral arguments are to be made in a request under sub‑paragraph ( a ) unless the appellate Court otherwise directs; and
-- src:2632 | ( c )
-- src:2633 | the Registrar of the Supreme Court may, upon receiving a request under sub‑paragraph ( a ), give directions on the making of written submissions for the request.
-- src:2634 | (9) The respondent must file and serve — ( a )
-- src:2635 | the respondent’s Case;
-- src:2636 | ( b )
-- src:2637 | the respondent’s core bundle of documents (if necessary); and
-- src:2638 | ( c )
-- src:2639 | the respondent’s bundle of authorities,
-- src:2640 | within 28 days after the appellant serves the documents mentioned in paragraph (4) or (5) on the respondent.
-- src:2641 | (10) Where the respondent fails to file and serve the respondent’s Case within the specified time, the respondent is not allowed to make submissions at the hearing of the appeal unless the appellate Court otherwise orders.
-- src:2642 | (11) The appellant must file and serve — ( a )
-- src:2643 | the appellant’s Reply (if any);
-- src:2644 | ( b )
-- src:2645 | the second core bundle (if necessary); and
-- src:2646 | ( c )
-- src:2647 | the appellant’s second bundle of authorities (if any),
-- src:2648 | within 14 days after the respondent’s Case is served on the appellant.
@ref O 19 r 30(4) (src:2595-2648)
GIVEN `o 19 r 30(11) there is a Reply, a second core bundle or a second bundle of authorities to file` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `o 19 duties party` `o 19 duties more act`
`o 19 r 30(4) the appellant must file and serve the appellant's documents within 8 weeks and the respondent and the appellant must follow` MEANS
    PARTY `o 19 r 14(1) the appellant`
    MUST `o 19 r 30(4) file and serve the documents mentioned in paragraph (4) or, on an appeal from the Appellate Division, paragraph (5)`
    WITHIN 56
    HENCE (
        PARTY `o 19 r 17(8) the respondent`
        MUST `o 19 r 30(9) file and serve the respondent's Case, the respondent's core bundle of documents (if necessary) and the respondent's bundle of authorities`
        WITHIN 28
        HENCE (
            IF `o 19 r 30(11) there is a Reply, a second core bundle or a second bundle of authorities to file`
            THEN (
                PARTY `o 19 r 14(1) the appellant`
                MUST `o 19 r 30(11) file and serve the appellant's Reply (if any), the second core bundle (if necessary) and the appellant's second bundle of authorities (if any)`
                WITHIN 14
                HENCE FULFILLED
                LEST BREACH BY `o 19 r 14(1) the appellant` BECAUSE "the appellant's Reply, second core bundle or second bundle of authorities was not filed and served within 14 days after the respondent's Case was served (rule 30(11)); the text gives no consequence for this"
            )
            ELSE FULFILLED
        )
        LEST BREACH BY `o 19 r 17(8) the respondent` BECAUSE "the respondent did not file and serve the respondent's Case within the specified time, so the respondent is not allowed to make submissions at the hearing of the appeal unless the appellate Court otherwise orders (rule 30(10)); this is the text's consequence, not a wrong"
    )
    LEST BREACH BY `o 19 r 14(1) the appellant` BECAUSE "the appellant did not file and serve the record of appeal, the core bundle of documents or the appellant's Case within the specified time, so the appeal is deemed withdrawn unless the appellate Court otherwise orders (rule 30(6)); this is the text's consequence, not a wrong"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rules 35 and 36 -- applications to the appellate Court (14 days each)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Twins: `o 19 r 35(14) the summons and the supporting affidavit are filed and served as required`, `o 19 r 36 the application for permission is filed and served as required` (roc4-order-19-div-3.l4).
-- src:2742 | (14) The summons and the supporting affidavit mentioned in paragraph (13) must be filed and served by the applicant on the parties to the application within 14 days after service of the notice of the appeal on the applicant.
@ref O 19 r 35(14) (src:2742)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `o 19 duties more party` `o 19 duties more act`
`o 19 r 35(14) the applicant must file and serve the summons and the supporting affidavit within 14 days` MEANS
    PARTY `o 19 r 35(14) the applicant`
    MUST `o 19 r 35(14) file and serve the summons and the supporting affidavit`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 19 r 35(14) the applicant` BECAUSE "the summons and the supporting affidavit were not filed and served on the parties to the application within 14 days after service of the notice of the appeal on the applicant (rule 35(14))"

-- src:2746 | 36. An application for the permission of — ( a )
-- src:2747 | a Judge sitting in the Appellate Division under section 40(4)( b ) of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act, to make an application to discharge or vary any direction or order mentioned in section 40(4)( a ) of that Act; or
-- src:2748 | ( b )
-- src:2749 | a Judge sitting in the Court of Appeal under section 58(4)( b ) of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act, to make an application to discharge or vary any direction or order mentioned in section 58(4)( a ) of that Act,
-- src:2750 | must be filed and served on all parties who have an interest in the appeal within 14 days after the date on which that direction or order is made.
@ref O 19 r 36 (src:2746-2750)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `o 19 duties more party` `o 19 duties more act`
`o 19 r 36 the applicant must file and serve the application for permission within 14 days` MEANS
    PARTY `o 19 r 36 the applicant for the permission`
    MUST `o 19 r 36 file and serve the application for permission`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 19 r 36 the applicant for the permission` BECAUSE "the application was not filed and served on all parties who have an interest in the appeal within 14 days after the date on which the direction or order is made (rule 36)"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rules 17(9), 18(3), 30(10) and 31(3) -- the bars that name the respondent, as prohibitions`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Ruling N2: where a flat negative names who bears it, the prohibition is derived from the decision-function answer.
-- Each bar holds only when the respondent failed to do the thing the rule asks for and the Court has not ordered otherwise; both are inputs, and when the bar does not hold the rule has nothing to say, so it is FULFILLED.
-- A SHANT with no WITHIN has no deadline of its own; the text gives the bar no end other than the hearing, and none is added.
-- Twins: `o 19 r 17(9) the respondent is barred from making submissions at the hearing of the appeal`, `o 19 r 18(3) the respondent is barred from making the submissions mentioned in paragraph (2)(d)` (roc4-order-19-div-2.l4);
-- `o 19 r 30(10) the respondent is barred from making submissions at the hearing of the appeal`, `o 19 r 31(3) the respondent is barred from making the submissions mentioned in paragraph (2)(d)` (roc4-order-19-div-3.l4).
-- src:2410 | (9) Where the respondent fails to file and serve the respondent’s Case within the specified time, the respondent is not allowed to make submissions at the hearing of the appeal unless the appellate Court otherwise orders.
@ref O 19 r 17(9) (src:2410)
GIVEN `the respondent failed to file and serve the respondent's Case within the specified time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appellate Court otherwise orders` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `o 19 duties more party` `o 19 duties more act`
`o 19 r 17(9) the respondent shall not make submissions at the hearing of the appeal` MEANS
    IF `the respondent failed to file and serve the respondent's Case within the specified time` AND NOT (`the appellate Court otherwise orders`)
    THEN
        PARTY `o 19 r 17(9) the respondent`
        SHANT `o 19 r 17(9) make submissions at the hearing of the appeal`
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY `o 19 r 17(9) the respondent` BECAUSE "the respondent made submissions at the hearing of the appeal after failing to file and serve the respondent's Case within the specified time, and the appellate Court had not otherwise ordered (rule 17(9))"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:2459 | (3) Where the respondent fails to comply with the requirements in paragraph (2)( d ), the respondent is not allowed to make the submissions mentioned in paragraph (2)( d ) unless the Court otherwise orders.
@ref O 19 r 18(3) (src:2459)
GIVEN `the respondent fails to comply with the requirements in paragraph (2)(d)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court otherwise orders` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `o 19 duties more party` `o 19 duties more act`
`o 19 r 18(3) the respondent shall not make the submissions mentioned in paragraph (2)(d)` MEANS
    IF `the respondent fails to comply with the requirements in paragraph (2)(d)` AND NOT (`the Court otherwise orders`)
    THEN
        PARTY `o 19 r 17(9) the respondent`
        SHANT `o 19 r 18(3) make the submissions mentioned in paragraph (2)(d)`
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY `o 19 r 17(9) the respondent` BECAUSE "the respondent made the submissions mentioned in paragraph (2)(d) after failing to comply with the requirements in that paragraph, and the Court had not otherwise ordered (rule 18(3))"
    ELSE FULFILLED

